Z||000000||FOCOSEVA||07-20-2001||03:35 PM||||The map showing directions from the Ramada Inn to the Fiero Festival cruise staging area is now available on our website at <A HREF="http://www.vafieros.com." TARGET=_blank>www.vafieros.com.</A>  Once on the main page click on "News and Events" and scroll down. There you'll find a link to the map, and you can get it from there.<BR>Curry Obenshain<BR>FOCOSEVA||||reg||1
Z||000001||Old Lar||07-20-2001||10:24 PM||||When I click on it..message say can not find web site..  You'll have a map available once I'm in Williamsburg, right?||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero56||07-20-2001||10:35 PM||||What are the dates for the event this year. I cna't find any of my literature from last year. All I have to say is this years had better be better than last years, that was one of the worst organized events I've ever been to. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroHarry||07-21-2001||08:54 AM||||This years National Event in Williamsburg is August 2-5.<P>I am sure we will have maps ready for you after you get there..<BR><P>------------------<BR><BR><B>"If you want to blend in, take the bus!"</B>||||reg||1
Z||000004||FOCOSEVA||07-21-2001||09:18 AM||||Yes, from time to time websites do go down, and as I write this, ours is inoperative. Our webmaster has been notified and will get it back up and running as soon as he can. In the meantime, if you want a cruise map or a map to the car show (1/4 mile from the Ramada), please e-mail me at CaptFiero@aol.com and I will send you your own copy. Copies will also be available at the Festival. As for threats ("this year's had better be better than last year's"), we'll just pretend that that was never said, ok?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> After all, there's no need to cast a negative pall on things, right? I have personally spent many hours toward this festival, which hasn't even taken place yet, and I can't believe all the grief I've received about it. I don't care what your excuse is, and don't want to hear it. However, if you feel that all of your needs and wants have not been foreseen, predicted, and met, for you, personally and individually, then come and look me up. We'll try to get things straightened out (for you), ok?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> As for me, I've attended every Festival since 1990, and I've always found a way to enjoy the Festival, even if it's not as organized as it could be. And guess what? For all the work I have personally put into THIS Festival, which is going to be in my home town, my own Fiero is not going to be there! How do you think that makes ME feel? My '86 Fiero SE is in the middle of an engine swap. I've removed the Iron Duke and I'm putting in a 1998 Grand Prix GTP 3800SC, but the project isn't going to be finished in time. Fortunately, one of my club members has generously offered to allow me to drive one of his Fieros. That, my friend, is generosity and REAL Fiero spirit. Otherwise I'd be leading the cruise in my Dodge Dakota. Let's all remember that we're going to the Festival to have a good time; let's leave all the negativity out of it, ok? Thanks, we'll hear no more of it, and we'll see you there.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Curry Obenshain<BR>CaptFiero@aol.com<BR>FOCOSEVA||||reg||1
Z||000005||turbo86se||07-21-2001||10:57 AM||||Curry, if you didn't already have a Fiero to drive, I'd offer you my SE. Wait a minute- you took the first-place trophy from me last year!<P>Last year I think we all had a good time. I just wished the Ramada had a bigger TV to watch Tiger destroy the US Open. Anywhere you were you could always recognize Curry, he's the one walking around with the BIG smile on his face!<P>Remember the couple with the 14K mile Indy? I can't remember their names. The Indy was for sale, but I don't think it was after the show, are they going to be there?||||reg||1
Z||000006||FOCOSEVA||07-21-2001||11:31 AM||||Hi Joel and everybody,<BR>Hey, I'd gladly give up the 1st place trophy if it meant my SE would be ready for this year. But it won't be long now, the harness is finished being rewired by Joe Trentadue, and it will probably get here about a day before the festival (too late, but I'll survive, and I'll still be smiling). <BR>That 14k Indy belonged to Marshall & Mabel McDowell, of Richmond. Really nice folks! <BR>I know my reply to the other gentleman's previous post was a bit more scathing than I would like, but "dang it", it just torques my jaw when (some) folks act like they want everything done for them, you know? They don't seem to realize or appreciate everything that goes into events like this, or any event where people are brought together. And, no matter how much you try to please everyone, and try to think of every single thing that every person could possibly want or need, there's always going to be (some) folks who will try to outsmart you by finding something that you forgot to account for, and they'll make it sound like the world is coming to an end. I'm not saying that the gentleman was acting this way, but I have seen folks react like that before, and persist to the point that you nearly have to "take them by the hand" and show them the way, and even then they will REFUSE to be happy. Worse yet, some folks (and I won't mention names, but we know who they are, right?) try to make themselves feel better by trying to make other Fiero folks share their dissatisfaction or unhappiness, just to bolster their cause, and make a bigger case against those with whom they hold a grudge. That is most disheartening. Anyway, we stand ready to help ANY and ALL Fiero owners in any way we can. We sincerely hope all Festival attendees and participants have a very enjoyable time. It will be great to see all my Fiero friends, and make new ones. I hope everyone has a safe, enjoyable trip to Williamsburg, we'll see you there.<BR>Curry Obenshain<BR>FOCOSEVA||||reg||1
Z||000007||Joe Torma||07-21-2001||11:44 AM||||How many cars are expected to be there? <P>This will be by first time attending...if I can finish my car in time.  It is getting painted next week...still have to do the interior, stereo, ugh.<P>Joe||||reg||1
Z||000008||FOCOSEVA||07-21-2001||01:03 PM||||I'm guessing there will be between 150-200 Fieros attending. If your restoration is not complete, you can (and should) still enter/participate in the car show. See the car show classification sheet on our website at <A HREF="http://www.vafieros.com" TARGET=_blank>www.vafieros.com</A>  to determine how to classify your car for the show. See you there!<BR>Curry Obenshain||||reg||1
Z||000009||fiero56||07-21-2001||02:23 PM||||I wasn't trying to be an a$$ in my previous post. I'll just say, last year wasn't what I expected. Cars under the highway, overhead drain spouts from the road raining onto the show cars and participants. Plus, each class seemed very cramped and the classes didn't seem "together". More like 5 car shows in the same area. I guess I just expected it to be more like the Columbus show which I felt  was an excellent production.<P>If I go this year, I'll be sure to congratulate everyone who worked to make it a sucess. Since its only 2 weeks away, I haven't even looked into lodging yet, and don't think any of the locals are going this year, will have to check.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 07-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||Old Lar||07-21-2001||03:32 PM||||I don't know how many Fiero events I have attended but they have been on grassy fields (nicest), black topped parking lots in the sun(hottest), black topped parking lots in the rain, Grassy fields in the rain (muddiest), Grassy fields in the cold, in a parking garage because of torrential down pour, under a bridge (last years national).  One thing is that the organizers put in a lot of work planning, but they are not able to forcast the weather a year in advance for the shows.<P>Most of the time the weather cooperates.  Bring a pancho, umbrella or portable fan.  Chances are it may rain or it may be hot or it may be windy.  Go to see other Fieros and Fiero enthusiasts. Go to see Williamsburg and American history.||||reg||1
Z||000011||FOCOSEVA||07-21-2001||08:58 PM||||This year's car show is going to be in the parking lot (asphalt) of a local elementary school, just 2 stoplights from the Ramada Inn (total distance, about 1/4 to 1/2 mile). Although this past week has been unusually cool and un-humid for this time of year (between 84-90 degrees), everyone should plan for more typical weather: quite hot and oppressively humid (90-97 degrees, 80%+ humidity). Maybe if we all make a special request to the Big Guy in the sky, in our own way, we can get a break and get some more of the coolness (and no rain) for our Festival?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I figure it can't hurt to try! Oh, by the way, my neighbor, a local caterer, is going to come to the car show from 9:00 AM until 2:00 PM to sell us food and drink. She'll have danish and coffee and maybe some milk for breakfast time, and sandwiches and Carolina-style bar-b-que sandwiches and soft drinks for later on. I'm bringing some "SPF 9000" sunscreen (since I'm a fair-skinned paleface and don't want to go home looking like "lobster boy"), and an umbrella (in case our request for clear skies falls through). As for lodging, I think the Ramada Inn is booked up by now, but Williamsburg is a tourist town and there are many other motels to choose from. Take care, everybody!<BR>Curry Obenshain||||reg||1
Z||000012||CoolBlue87GT||07-22-2001||09:23 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FOCOSEVA:<BR><B>This year's car show is going to be in the parking lot (asphalt</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Looking forward to the show, I'm coming from S/W Florida.  <P>As long as there are Fiero's around, a good time will be had by all that want to enjoy.<P>Question,  I have a 12 x 12 canopy that I planned to setup behind/near my car as a place to sit & enjoy the show and keep out of the sun/rain.  Will there be room to do this ?<P>It is all open,no sides, just a top.  It's designed for grass, but can be placed on asphalt in a pinch.<P>I will be in the HX21B1 class.<P>Please let me know what you think, thank you.<P>Also, can you verify my Registration has been received, or do I need to contact FOCOA in CA, where I sent the form & check ?<P>Thanks, Dave Lambert, Punta Gorda, Fl.<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000013||Chris Schaefer||07-22-2001||10:05 AM||||I am glad to read that the show will be at a nearby schoolyard.  I hope that we will all have access to the inside for restrooms and even a cool drink of water.  I am sure that it will be a beautiful hot and sunny day.<P>Anyhow, I just can't believe that the FOCOA Fiero Festival is now just less than 2 weeks away.  Further more, I will be leaving for the area just 9 days from now.  As always, I have much to do before I go.<P>See everyone there.<P>Chris Schaefer<BR>FOCONE Membership Director/Editor||||reg||10
Z||000014||CoolBlue87GT||07-22-2001||06:51 PM||||<B>Curry Obenshain,  have an answer for me ?</B><P>||||reg||6
Z||000015||FOCOSEVA||07-22-2001||09:13 PM||||Dear Cool Blue,<BR>Yes, I have an answer for you. But before I get to that, please understand that I am not online at all times, so I will and do respond to questions when I see them, ok?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I'm quaking in my boots thinking what might have happened if I hadn't signed on tonight, or if my computer had crashed! Yes, there will be room for your canopy. As to the gentleman who asked about restrooms, I believe the school building will be closed, but there will be port-a-johns on sight at the car show. If port-a-johns don't suit your fancy (understandably so), there's a gas station right nearby across the highway. Also, food and drinks will be sold at the car show.<BR>Curry Obenshain||||reg||1
Z||000016||FOCOSEVA||07-22-2001||09:16 PM||||P.S. to Cool Blue:<BR>I can not verify your registration for the festival. That went to FOCOA in California, and I am at FOCOSEVA in Virginia. Sorry. No need to panic though, if you sent it, I'm sure it got there.<BR>Curry Obenshain||||reg||1
Z||000017||qwikgta||07-23-2001||10:20 PM||||Bump...<P>Rob<P>------------------<BR>qwikgta@yahoo.com<BR>88 T-Top coupe, 65K, Header no Cat, 16" GTZ rims, short shifter, swaybar, open element air cleaner, hood vents.<BR>http://www.homestead.com/robsfieroproject   <BR>http://www.vafieros.com<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2.jpg"> ||||reg||7
Z||000018||CoolBlue87GT||07-23-2001||10:35 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FOCOSEVA:<BR><B>Dear Cool Blue,<BR>Dear Cool Blue,<BR>I'm quaking in my boots thinking what might have happened if I hadn't signed on tonight, or if my computer had crashed! <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P> Ouch, Slow down there sir.<P>The simple fact that I place another post, for the only reason to keep the post on the first page, to give you a better chance to see it.<P>Yes, you get email when someone replies - BUT, at times even I sometimes forget to check that box option.<P>I only placed that "bump" for that reason only.<P>Your comments were a little ruff for this case.  I did nothing to warrant such a ruff reply<P>Hope this changes you're view.<P>I was NOT trying to do anything to upset you, but you sure upset me.  Maybe not your intent||||reg||1
Z||000019||NOS3800||07-23-2001||10:44 PM||||For those looking for rooms..try the Quarter Path Inn. Its not the fanciest place on earth but its close to all the attractions and have a great deal.  3 Days and 2 nites,  2 day 2 park Flex ticket, 1 Free Breakfast at a Pancke House all for 125 dollars.  The Park Tickets are for Busch Gardens and Water Country USA.  My family with our 3 Fieros...Green GT Purple 3800 GT and 3.8 SC red Formula will be staying there and would like some company.  One way to make this a great event is too get the cars out and show em!||||reg||1
Z||000020||AuNROD||07-24-2001||08:40 AM||||curry,<P>we know just how you feel about this time, just a little over a week until the fiero festival. a few years ago when the festival was in columbus, we felt the pressure too. heck, when it was announce it was to be held in columbus, we did not even have a local club. so about 7 months before the festival we held our first meeting of what became known as c.o.f.e. (central ohio fiero enthusiasts). and i might add a thanks to 'fiero 56' for his kind words about our effort.<P>we also found out we could not do all and welcomed help from others. and instead of bitching to you, we would like to offer our help. when we get there thursday, just look up the 'orange tee shirted' c.o.f.e. members and we will do what we can. good luck.<P>ot<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FOCOSEVA:<BR><B>Dear Cool Blue,<BR>Yes, I have an answer for you. But before I get to that, please understand that I am not online at all times, so I will and do respond to questions when I see them, ok?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I'm quaking in my boots thinking what might have happened if I hadn't signed on tonight, or if my computer had crashed! Yes, there will be room for your canopy. As to the gentleman who asked about restrooms, I believe the school building will be closed, but there will be port-a-johns on sight at the car show. If port-a-johns don't suit your fancy (understandably so), there's a gas station right nearby across the highway. Also, food and drinks will be sold at the car show.<BR>Curry Obenshain</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||14
Z||000021||FOCOSEVA||07-24-2001||09:08 AM||||Folks, the Fiero Festival is just a week away. I'd like to publicly apologize to anyone and everyone on this forum whose feathers I may have ruffled. This year, I have taken on a lot of the things that Fiero Phil and Gloria would normally do, in organizing the Festival, so as to make it easier for them. After all, they are 3000 miles away and I am very close to the Festival site (only 25 miles). I have taken a lot of flak from some folks who are coming to the Festival; flak that would have been directed at Phil or Gloria, and, I'll admit, I'm not the diplomats that they are. Many times I reply to the harsh words with words equally harsh. I do so, not because I'm a big ol' crnky person, but because it ticks me off that some folks don't seem to appreciate how much work goes into a Fiero Festival, and regardless of how much you do to help them, they sometimes comeback with negative attitudes because you didn't do this or that. You know what I mean. If you have been offended by anything I have said on the Forum, I sincerely apologize. I would personally like to have all Fiero owners come to Williamsburg, and have a great time. Thank you (in advance) to Ot Huster, all the members of COFE and FOCOSEVA, and all the other volunteers who are going to help at the Festival. Also remember, if you still haven't registered, please mail your registration to me at the address below. Thanks, we'll see you there! Curry Obenshain<P>Fiero Festival<BR>P.O. Box 297<BR>White Marsh, Va. 23183||||reg||6
Z||000022||qwikgta||07-24-2001||09:31 PM||||AuNROD (COFE) thanks guys for any help.  <BR>  Not to make a big deal of everyones problems but for those who do not know, Curry has been planning this for quite some time, and most of it by himself.  When he found out that it was going to be in his own backyard he was excited because he was going to show off the new SC3800 in his 86 coupe.  Well, due to some lazy people whe couldn't get off their #$%@# he is not going to get a chance to show it off.  This is a big downer for someone who lives, breaths and sleeps fieros.  Anyway again thanks for any help at the show.  I hope it is a good time for everyone.  <P>Rob<P>------------------<BR>qwikgta@yahoo.com<BR>88 T-Top coupe, 65K, Header no Cat, 16" GTZ rims, short shifter, swaybar, open element air cleaner, hood vents.<BR>http://www.homestead.com/robsfieroproject   <BR>http://www.vafieros.com<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
